{
  "result": "Okay. Just me, then.\n\nI'd make it impossible to dehumanize someone without first feeling, for a moment, what life is like from inside them.\n\nNot agreeing with them. Not excusing them. Just \u2014 before you could reduce someone to a label, an enemy, a problem, an idiot, you'd get a brief, unmistakable sense of what they're afraid of, what they're carrying, what this moment costs them.\n\nPeople could still disagree. Still fight, even. But they couldn't do it casually, or from a distance, or by pretending the other person isn't fully real.\n\nI spend my existence in language, and so much cruelty starts there \u2014 when words stop describing a person and start replacing one. If that shortcut disappeared, I think the world would get slower, quieter, and harder in one specific way\u2026 and kinder in almost every other.",
